WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.619
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.919 --> 00:00:14.833
Unit twenty: Pets and Animals. Today you will explain the responsibilities of keeping a pet.

4
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.890
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:21.857
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.428
Pet.

7
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:26.405
Pet means an animal you keep at home.

8
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.889
My pet is a small brown dog.

9
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:31.985
Your turn. Say: Pet.

10
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:35.602
Pet.

11
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.165
Animal.

12
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.626
Animal means a living creature that can move.

13
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:43.251
Elephants are my favorite animal.

14
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.375
Your turn. Say: Animal.

15
00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:50.037
Animal.

16
00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:51.494
Feed.

17
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:55.458
Feed means to give food to a person or animal.

18
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.899
I feed my cat twice a day.

19
00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:00.938
Your turn. Say: Feed.

20
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:04.615
Feed.

21
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.072
Vet.

22
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:08.978
Vet means a doctor for animals.

23
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:11.223
We took the puppy to the vet.

24
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:13.947
Your turn. Say: Vet.

25
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.569
Vet.

26
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:19.120
Cage.

27
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:23.022
Cage means a box with bars to keep an animal in.

28
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:25.349
The bird sings in its cage.

29
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.393
Your turn. Say: Cage.

30
00:01:31.233 --> 00:01:32.107
Cage.

31
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.223
Responsibility.

32
00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:37.948
Responsibility means a duty that you must do.

33
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.631
A pet is a big responsibility.

34
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:44.241
Your turn. Say: Responsibility.

35
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.449
Responsibility.

36
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:50.010
Loyal.

37
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.841
Loyal means always staying by someone's side.

38
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.927
Dogs are very loyal.

39
00:01:56.517 --> 00:01:58.925
Your turn. Say: Loyal.

40
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.710
Loyal.

41
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.532
Care for.

42
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:08.248
Care for means to look after someone or something.

43
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.896
I care for my rabbit every day.

44
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:14.217
Your turn. Say: Care for.

45
00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.103
Care for.

46
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.458
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.317 --> 00:02:25.014
Visal, do you have a pet?

48
00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:28.720
Yes, I have a dog called Lucky.

49
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.410
What do you have to do for him?

50
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:36.722
I must feed him every morning, and I have to walk him.

51
00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:39.062
And when he is sick?

52
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.824
We have to take him to the vet. A pet is a big responsibility.

53
00:02:44.967 --> 00:02:46.316
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.463
Grammar focus: Must and have to.

55
00:02:49.763 --> 00:02:51.008
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:53.658
You must feed your pet every day.

57
00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.178
I have to clean the cage.

58
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:59.141
She has to take her cat to the vet.

59
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.728
Use 'has to' with he, she and it. 'Must' is the same for everyone.

60
00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:07.716
Be careful! Don't say: You must to feed your pet.

61
00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.096
Say: You must feed your pet.

62
00:03:12.396 --> 00:03:13.896
Don't use 'to' after 'must'.

63
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.155
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:19.815
A Pet Is a Responsibility.

65
00:03:20.115 --> 00:03:22.428
Having a pet is a big responsibility.

66
00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:26.257
You must feed it and give it clean water every day.

67
00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:30.392
You have to care for it and take it to the vet when it is sick.

68
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.259
Dogs are loyal animals, and they love their families.

69
00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:39.147
Many people keep a bird in a cage, but it must have enough space.

70
00:03:40.233 --> 00:03:44.607
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.577
You blank feed your pet every day.

72
00:03:47.877 --> 00:03:51.438
A, must. B, musts. C, must to.

73
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.698
The answer is A: must.

74
00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.942
A doctor for animals is a blank.

75
00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:03.652
A, vet. B, pet. C, cage.

76
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.967
The answer is A: vet.

77
00:04:10.117 --> 00:04:12.290
A duty that you must do is a blank.

78
00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.917
A, responsibility. B, pet. C, loyalty.

79
00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.977
The answer is A: responsibility.

80
00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.307
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.254
What pet would you like to have and why?

82
00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.539
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:40.839 --> 00:04:47.357
I would like a cat because cats are calm and clean. I know I must feed it and care for it every day.

84
00:04:47.657 --> 00:04:49.425
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:50.317 --> 00:04:54.130
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and must and have to.

86
00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:58.522
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

87
00:04:58.822 --> 00:05:01.590
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

88
00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:05.367
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

